```js
export function solve(stock, items) {
  const original = { ...stock };
  const remaining = { ...original };

  try {
    for (const { sku, quantity } of items) {
      if (
        !Number.isInteger(quantity) ||
        quantity <= 0 ||
        (remaining[sku] ?? 0) < quantity
      ) {
        throw Error("rejected");
      }
      remaining[sku] -= quantity;
    }
    return { accepted: true, stock: remaining };
  } catch {
    return { accepted: false, stock: original };
  }
}
```

This restores all-or-nothing reservation: deductions accumulate only in the working copy, including for duplicate SKUs. Success returns that copy; rejection returns unchanged original quantities. The caller’s stock is never mutated.

